00:02:34.707 --> 00:02:39.050
<v Orlando>Now, José Luis, in Venezuela, however,
did you go maternal, paternal?

00:02:39.100 --> 00:02:42.800
<v José Luis>That's right. My name is José Luis Montiel Huerta.

00:02:42.850 --> 00:02:45.300
<v Orlando>So there we do it the other way around.

00:02:45.350 --> 00:02:46.800
<v José Luis>Montiel because my father.

00:02:46.850 --> 00:02:51.050
<v José Luis>Huerta because my mother. We honor the mother

00:02:51.100 --> 00:02:52.810
<v José Luis>and we carry her maiden name.

00:02:52.860 --> 00:02:56.790
<v Orlando>So in Latin America, it's generally the
paternal name followed by the maternal.

00:02:56.840 --> 00:02:59.630
<v Orlando>In Brazil, it's the other way around, maternal, paternal.

00:02:59.680 --> 00:03:02.800
